Hi all,

I tried btcreate option & it worked smoothly.
Following are the details:

a. Took the btcreate of existing 9GB OS disk.
b. prepared the new RAID1 of 2x 72GB Disks
c. prepared partitions for OS in the new Disk through diskconfig.
d. Removed the existing OS disk from the Server
e. From console I run P00>>>boot -fl "nc" mka500
f. used Advanced option while restoration. It asked for all the
available disks where restoration can be done.
g. Selected the required Disk & then the partition for SWAP, ROOT,
USR/VAR.
h. Booted the Server with new RAID Disk
i. changed the /etc/fdmns links for the Data Disks.
j. Once OS disk is moved from 9GB to new RAID disk, OS was upgraded from
5.1A to 5.1B-2 through "installupdate" utility.

This was a very simple & straight forward solution.

Thanks & regards.
Vimal=20

